    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Research this application for the Composio integration audit.\n\nApp: {{ $json.app }}\nCategory: {{ $json.category }}\nHint URL: {{ $json.hint_url }}\n\nUse Tavily to search current official documentation.\n\nReturn only these research facts:\n\n1. Description\n2. Authentication methods: return ONLY short controlled tokens from this set — OAuth2, API Key, Basic Auth, Token, Other. Do not include descriptions, flow names, or parenthetical detail here.\n3. Auth notes: any nuance on authentication — which OAuth flows, token scoping, CLI-issued tokens, session vs long-lived credentials, etc. — goes here instead of in field 2.\n4. How credentials are obtained\n5. Access model: self-serve / paid / admin-gated / partner-gated / contact-sales / unknown\n6. API type\n7. API breadth: broad / medium / narrow / unknown\n8. Official or credible MCP availability: yes / no / unknown\n9. Buildability: buildable / blocked / unclear\n10. Main blocker\n11. Evidence URLs\n12. Confidence: high / medium / low\n13. Status: researched / needs_review / failed\n\nRules:\n- Prioritize official developer documentation.\n- Do not guess.\n- API existence does not prove self-serve access.\n- OAuth does not prove that credentials are freely obtainable.\n- An ordinary API is not an MCP server.\n- Field 2 (Authentication methods) must contain ONLY tokens from the controlled set, comma-separated if more than one applies — no sentences, no parentheses, no flow names.\n- Keep every answer concise.\n- Return evidence URLs for important claims.\n\nStatus rules:\n- Use \"researched\" when sufficient evidence is found for the requested fields.\n- Use \"needs_review\" when important information is unclear, conflicting, or unavailable.\n- Use \"failed\" only when the research/search process fails and usable evidence cannot be obtained.\n\nDo not mark an application \"researched\" simply because an API exists.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
